      },
      {
        "text": "To justify actions against certain beings, those beings must be portrayed as non-human or partially non-human.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "A fetus will eventually develop into a full human being if allowed to progress naturally.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The argument that a fetus is merely a clump of cells or an embryo rather than a human being is commonly used to justify certain positions.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "People who cannot survive independently are still considered living beings.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Some individuals, such as newborns and people with severe disabilities, cannot survive independently.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Justifying abortion requires denying that a developing fetus is human life.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "It would be problematic to conclude that someone who cannot survive alone is not truly alive.",
